💡Docker Cheatsheet

💥Docker Basics

→ docker --version → Check Docker version
→ docker info → Display Docker system information
→ docker help → Show Docker help menu
→ docker version → Display client and server versions

💥Images

→ docker pull → Download an image
→ docker images → List local images
→ docker build → Build image from Dockerfile
→ docker tag → Tag an image
→ docker push → Push image to registry
→ docker rmi → Remove an image
→ docker image prune → Remove unused images

💥Containers

→ docker run → Create and start a container
→ docker ps → List running containers
→ docker ps -a → List all containers
→ docker start → Start a stopped container
→ docker stop → Stop a running container
→ docker restart → Restart a container
→ docker rm → Remove a container
→ docker rename → Rename a container
→ docker exec → Execute command inside container
→ docker attach → Attach to a running container

💥Logs & Monitoring

→ docker logs → View container logs
→ docker stats → Monitor resource usage
→ docker top → Show running processes
→ docker inspect → View detailed container information
→ docker events → Stream Docker events

💥Volumes

→ docker volume create → Create a volume
→ docker volume ls → List volumes
→ docker volume inspect → View volume details
→ docker volume rm → Remove a volume
→ docker volume prune → Remove unused volumes

💥Networks

→ docker network ls → List networks
→ docker network create → Create network
→ docker network inspect → Inspect network
→ docker network connect → Connect container to network
→ docker network disconnect → Disconnect container
→ docker network rm → Remove network

💥Docker Compose

→ docker compose up → Start services
→ docker compose down → Stop and remove services
→ docker compose ps → List services
→ docker compose logs → View service logs
→ docker compose build → Build services
→ docker compose restart → Restart services
→ docker compose exec → Run command in service

💥Dockerfile

→ FROM → Base image
→ WORKDIR → Set working directory
→ COPY → Copy files into image
→ ADD → Copy files and URLs
→ RUN → Execute command during build
→ CMD → Default container command
→ ENTRYPOINT → Main executable
→ ENV → Set environment variables
→ EXPOSE → Document exposed port
→ VOLUME → Create mount point
→ USER → Set execution user
→ LABEL → Add image metadata

💥Cleanup

→ docker system df → Show Docker disk usage
→ docker system prune → Remove unused resources
→ docker container prune → Remove stopped containers
→ docker image prune → Remove dangling images
→ docker volume prune → Remove unused volumes
→ docker network prune → Remove unused networks

💥Advanced

→ docker save → Export image to archive
→ docker load → Import image archive
→ docker export → Export container filesystem
→ docker import → Create image from archive
→ docker cp → Copy files between host and container
→ docker diff → Show container filesystem changes
→ docker history → Show image layer history
